lantern-pr 1
# 33
#title Make six brittle tests derive their expectations from the source
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/33
#branch chore/robust-brittle-tests
#base main
#opened 2026-11-11
#head 22c4fa26190ce84c9da064b6396d25c6ca494032
#describe what Six brittle tests now derive expectations from the command registry, the skill bundle, model-floor.json and the real handlers.
#describe before Hard-coded 20-command and 16-skill lists, counted regex matches in main.ts.
#describe after Lists come from the source of truth; wiring is checked by where a call sits.
#describe verified typecheck, lint and the full test run are green; each contract was broken in source and its test failed.
+ test/helpers/source-blocks.ts
~ test/editor-demand-wiring.test.ts
~ test/install-skills.test.ts
~ test/lantern-macro-load.test.ts
~ test/lantern-permissions-triggers.test.ts
~ test/lantern-sync-selftest.test.ts
~ test/project-window.test.ts
#order test/helpers/source-blocks.ts
#order test/editor-demand-wiring.test.ts
#order test/lantern-permissions-triggers.test.ts
#order test/lantern-macro-load.test.ts
#order test/project-window.test.ts
#order test/install-skills.test.ts
#order test/lantern-sync-selftest.test.ts
#reason test/helpers/source-blocks.ts Shared bracket matcher so wiring tests locate handlers and function bodies without brittle regexes.
#reason test/editor-demand-wiring.test.ts Asserts where editor-server calls sit instead of counting regex matches, so renames and reorders do not break it.
#reason test/install-skills.test.ts Takes the skill list from the bundle and the skills folder instead of a hand-kept list of sixteen.
#reason test/lantern-macro-load.test.ts Drops the literal block and edge counts and checks the handler wiring by location, not exact text.
#reason test/lantern-permissions-triggers.test.ts Checks that saving the linker or importing a list syncs rules by calling the real handlers.
#reason test/lantern-sync-selftest.test.ts Drives the model policy check from model-floor.json instead of a pinned list of ids and a sentence.
#reason test/project-window.test.ts Expects the registry's commands to be registered instead of a hand-kept list of command names.
#story Tests stop breaking on unrelated edits
#step actor A developer renames or reorders code
#file test/helpers/source-blocks.ts
#step action runs the test suite
#step subject the six rewritten tests
#file test/editor-demand-wiring.test.ts
#file test/project-window.test.ts
#file test/install-skills.test.ts
#below interaction Sees a failure only when a real contract breaks
#file test/lantern-permissions-triggers.test.ts
#file test/lantern-macro-load.test.ts
#file test/lantern-sync-selftest.test.ts
#below consequence A new command or skill needed a list edit => The list comes from the registry or bundle
